Subject: original-generation components: class style hooks, overlay roles, fixes

What: every original-generation component the app loads carries `ui-*` class hooks
next to its data attributes and its sheet selects the classes; overlays paint from
the semantic overlay roles; spacing uses logical properties so RTL mirrors; type and
radius come from theme tokens; plus component fixes (card's opt-in accent rail,
select's settings trigger, text-shimmer mounting its swept copy only while sweeping,
toast actions, list search action inside the field, ...).
Why: Blink buckets a rule by its rightmost class, so a class-keyed rule is tried only
on elements carrying that class, while every `[data-component]`/`[data-slot]` rule
shares one attribute bucket tried on every element with the attribute.

